#  Restaurant Menu & Order Management System (Python Assignment Part 2)

##  Description
This project is a command-line based Restaurant Order Management System built using Python data structures such as dictionaries, lists, and nested data.  
It simulates menu handling, cart operations, inventory tracking, and sales analysis.

---

##  Features

###  Task 1: Menu Exploration
- Displayed menu grouped by category (Starters, Mains, Desserts)
- Counted total items and available items
- Identified most expensive item
- Listed items priced under ₹150

---

###  Task 2: Cart Operations
- Added items to cart with quantity
- Checked availability before adding
- Updated quantity for duplicate items
- Removed items from cart
- Calculated subtotal, GST (5%), and total bill

---

###  Task 3: Inventory Tracker (Deep Copy)
- Created a deep copy of inventory using copy.deepcopy()
- Deducted stock after order placement
- Displayed reorder alerts for low stock items
- Verified backup inventory remains unchanged

---

###  Task 4: Sales Log Analysis
- Calculated total revenue per day
- Identified best-selling day
- Found most ordered items
- Added new sales data and updated results
- Printed numbered list of all orders

---

## Technologies Used
- Python 3
- Data Structures (List, Dictionary)
- copy module (Deep Copy)

